            <ArticleTitle>Indolyl-naphthyl-maleimides as potent and selective inhibitors of protein kinase C-α/β.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>781-786</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0960-894X(17)30050-1</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.bmcl.2017.01.038</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The indolyl-naphthyl maleimide 7 is a potent inhibitor of the classical PKC isotypes α,β and shows excellent selectivity over the novel PKC isotypes δ,ε,η,θ and other kinases belonging to the AGC family. The SAR around 7 as well as the physico-chemical characteristics of selected derivatives and their activity in T and B cell activation and proliferation assays are discussed.</AbstractText>
